,\" to look for the effects of an electrical injury. They’ll also ask about what happened. If you can’t tell them, they’ll ask someone who was with you or first responders.\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"44673bbef5d2_mobile_ad\",{\"data-identity\":\"billboard-ad\",\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden print:hidden max-w-[400px] min-w-[300px] m-auto items-center justify-center bg-gray-300 pt-rem16px pb-[3.125rem] my-rem32px  \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-[300px] mx-auto\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 uppercase text-rem10px leading-rem16px mx-auto w-fit\",\"children\":\"Advertisement"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden flex-col items-center justify-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"ad-slot\",\"id\":\"billboard3_300x250_mobile\",\"className\":\"ad-reset w-[300px] !min-h-[250px] flex bg-gray-300\"}],null]}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"0f1ec39473f5\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"There are several tests healthcare providers will likely use. These don’t diagnose an electrical injury. Instead, the tests look for signs of related injuries or complications. The tests they’ll likely use include:\"]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",\"49e649cc3d71-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"49e649cc3d71\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",\"51f09371a9c6\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diagnostics/16953-electrocardiogram-ekg\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"Electrocardiogram (EKG)\"]}],\" to check your heart for damage or irregular rhythms\"]}],\"$L6e\",\"$L6f\"]}]]}]]}],false]}]\n52:[\"$\",\"div\",\"35f898c23726603eb8fa5e2101c9db49\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"article-section\",\"id\":\"management-and-treatment\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[112px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem34px text-rem32px bp600:text-rem40px bp600:leading-rem44px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold mt-rem56px print:mt-rem24px mb-rem16px print:mb-rem8px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold break-words\",\"children\":\"Management and Treatment\"}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"rich-text\",\"className\":\" after:content-[''] after:table\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"b2c7c4f8d1d4\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"How is an electric shock treated?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"186a0961914a\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Treatment for electric shocks starts with first aid. If you’re with someone who’s being shocked and they can’t let go or pull away, you should do the following:\"]}],[\"$\",\"ol\",\"e07c55f47b0c-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"ordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-rem24px list-decimal marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal marker:text-brandBlue-500 marker:font-semibold print:marker:text-black  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"e07c55f47b0c\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"c3a2ab978eeb\",{\"children\":[\"Don’t get shocked yourself\"]}],\": Don’t directly touch anything electrified, including the person being shocked. Turn off the power if you can. If you can’t, try to separate them from what’s shocking them. Break the connection with something nonconductive, like wood, plastic or cardboard.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"0e455c52b13b\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,":text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"df9450d6ada2\",{\"children\":[\"Get help\"]}],\": Call 911 (or your local emergency services number) immediately.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"93e3be694fd0\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"15e95ea87904\",{\"children\":[\"Start first aid\"]}],\":\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"4dd8b9640ee3\",{\"children\":[\" \"]}],\"Check their breathing and pulse. Start CPR if you don’t find either of those. If they have a pulse and are breathing, put them in the \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"9cb1e7997723\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/first-aid\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"recovery position\"]}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"9c57c2594bc7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"$L70\",\":\",\"$L71\",\"Move them as little as possible. The only exception is if not moving them would put you or them in harm’s way. Examples include if you need to do CPR or if you need to move them away from something dangerous, like a downed power line.\"]}]]}],\"$L72\",\"$L73\",\"$L74\",\"$L75\",\"$L76\",\"$L77\",\"$L78\",\"$L79\",\"$L7a\"]}]]}],\"$L7b\"]}]\n53:[\"$\",\"div\",\"edec8ec9a5affaedaffd410327dcbd3c\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"article-section\",\"id\":\"outlook-prognosis\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[112px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem34px text-rem32px bp600:text-rem40px bp600:leading-rem44px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold mt-rem56px print:mt-rem24px mb-rem16px print:mb-rem8px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold break-words\",\"children\":\"Outlook / Prognosis\"}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"rich-text\",\"className\":\" after:content-[''] after:table\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"cf79cd2c7da6\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"What can I expect if I receive an electric shock?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"15ee8f6697f0\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Electric shocks can range from very mild to severe and fatal. The outlook depends on many factors, especially details like the source of electricity, how long the shock lasted, voltage and amperage, and your health history.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"c29ef997a60f\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Because there are many factors at play, your healthcare provider is the best person to tell you what you can expect.\"]}]]}]]}],false]}]\n54:[\"$\",\"div\",\"275b1ea9af5555e1c6cd9c58208cd677\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"article-section\",\"id\":\"prevention\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[112px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem34px text-rem32px bp600:text-rem40px bp600:leading-rem44px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold mt-rem56px print:mt-rem24px mb-rem16px print:mb-rem8px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold break-words\",\"children\":\"Prevention\"}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"rich-text\",\"className\":\" after:content-[''] af"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ter:table\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"1cf82c8e7db7\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Are electric shocks preventable?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"de4b16d7874f\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Yes, electric shocks are extremely preventable. Here are some things you can do:\"]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",\"3b70374a2831-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"3b70374a2831\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Never touch power lines, even if they don’t look like they’re live.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"883b12905fcb\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Don’t use damaged or fraying electrical cords (or devices that have them).\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"5d228d496792\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Stay away from downed power lines and don’t drive through water near one.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"1ccd23cb4867\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Don’t use electrical devices, switches or outlets when you’re wet or standing in water.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"75030aadb9fd\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Protect children by keeping electrical cords out of reach (so they can’t be chewed) and covering electrical outlets.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"d069a2476c0b\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Turn off electricity at the circuit breaker before doing your own electrical work.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"e484cff5d94d\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Turn to professionals for jobs that are higher-risk or that could be above your skill level, like tree-trimming, appliance repairs or household electric work.\"]}],\"$L7c\",\"$L7d\"]}]]}]]}],false]}]\n55:[\"$\",\"div\",\"9b41a0eeca062cc9e9948563a66e5da2\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"article-section\",\"id\":\"additional-common-questions\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[112px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem34px text-rem32px bp600:text-rem40px bp600:leading-rem44px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold mt-rem56px print:mt-rem24px mb-rem16px print:mb-rem8px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold break-words\",\"children\":\"Additional Common Questions\"}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"rich-text\",\"className\":\" after:content-[''] after:table\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"2f285a00b285\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold m"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"t-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"What is the difference between electrocution vs. an electric shock?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"3f343982aacf\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Not everyone uses these terms the same way.\"]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",\"f5b6f2678cfe-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"f5b6f2678cfe\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"82270c2ad0ad\",{\"children\":[\"Electrocution \"]}],\"always refers to death or serious injury from electricity. But some experts and organizations only use it when referring to deaths.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"d1d6012ab60c\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"ce94a4b76349\",{\"children\":[\"Electric shocks\"]}],\" always involve contact with electricity. But they don’t always cause harm.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",\"6d949000c769\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Can an electric shock from a plug kill you?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"3e73be541e7e\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Yes, but it doesn’t happen very often. In the U.S., electrical outlets are on 120-volt circuits (240-volt circuits for larger appliances like clothes dryers). That’s enough to cause serious injury or death under the right circumstances.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"dd84549ae565\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"This is where GFCI outlets can make a huge difference in protecting you from outlet-related shocks. They automatically cut off electricity at much lower levels than a circuit breaker or fuse. That can save you from serious harm or worse.\"]}],\"$L7e\",\"$L7f\"]}]]}],false]}]\n56:[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px print:mt-rem12px print:mb-rem8px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold\",\"children\":\"A note from Cleveland Clinic\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"rich-text\",\"className\":\" after:content-[''] after:table\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"649f7c039777\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Maybe you shocked yourself while trying to jump-start a car or using an electric cord that you didn’t realize was frayed. You might find yourself wondering what to do next, or if there’s a chance you might need to go to the hospital.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"66727b9b8b14\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Most of the time, electr"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ic shocks are minor and don’t cause dangerous effects. But it’s important to remember that electric shocks can cause damage inside your body that you can’t see. When in doubt, it’s best to err on the side of caution. Call your healthcare provider or go to the hospital after you get shocked. Getting care quickly can catch any issues you might have and help set your mind at ease.\"]}]]}]]\n57:[[\"$\",\"$L80\",\"0\",{\"title\":\"Better health starts here\",\"blurb\":\"Sign up for our Health Essentials emails for expert guidance on nutrition, fitness, sleep, skin care and more.\",\"cadence\":null,\"iconImage\":\"https://assets.clevelandclinic.org/transform/482db8cd-aa1e-45b5-a2a4-cf6aa5e5d2d4/Health-Essentials\",\"secondaryLogo\":{\"alt\":\"Health Essentials logo\",\"width\":200,\"height\":40,\"linkHref\":\"https://health.clevelandclinic.org/\",\"sizes\":\"150px, (min-width: 600px) 200px\",\"className\":\"w-[150px] h-[30px] bp600:w-[200px] bp600:h-[40px]\",\"logoType\":\"health-essentials\"},\"buttonText\":\" Sign up\",\"buttonUrl\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health-essentials-sign-up\",\"buttonNewTab\":false,\"exampleEmailLink\":\"https://assets.clevelandclinic.org/transform/2ff943a2-abb1-4a1c-8ede-f8848703e789/HealthEssentials-SampleEmail-2026\",\"exampleEmailText\":\"Example email\",\"emailNewTab\":true,\"className\":\"mt-rem56px print:hidden\"}]]\n58:[[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-blue-050 p-rem32px pb-rem8px mt-rem56px print:hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mb-rem16px\",\"children\":\"Ex